# Template for the local .env. Copy it and fill in the key:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     source tools/load-env.sh
#
# This file is committed and holds no secret. `.env` is not: it is gitignored,
# `make guard` refuses it, and a pre-commit hook refuses it again for the
# `git add -f` case. `make clean` never deletes it.
#
# caudit itself does not read this file. The shell exports what is below and
# caudit reads the environment, at call time, as it always has.
#
# GOOGLE_API_KEY is accepted as a fallback; GEMINI_API_KEY is checked first.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# A key alone transmits nothing. Sending source to a hosted model also needs
# explicit consent -- `caudit scan --consent-cloud`, or `--remember-consent`
# to record it in .caudit/cloud-consent.json. See my_docs/guides/setup.md section 5.
